WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.201 --> 00:00:03.636
-The president met with
the leader of Hungary

00:00:03.636 --> 00:00:05.038
while he was feuding with China,

00:00:05.038 --> 00:00:06.772
and his lawyer
was trying to get Ukraine

00:00:06.772 --> 00:00:08.374
to meddle in the 2020 election.

00:00:08.374 --> 00:00:10.743
For more on this, it's time
for "A Closer Look.'

00:00:10.743 --> 00:00:12.178
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:12.178 --> 00:00:14.580 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:14.580 --> 00:00:17.316
-Trump met today with
the Prime Minister of Hungary,

00:00:17.316 --> 00:00:20.419
Viktor Orbán, a far-right
authoritarian strongman

00:00:20.419 --> 00:00:22.288
who has curtailed democracy
in his country,

00:00:22.288 --> 00:00:24.290
has almost total control
of the media,

00:00:24.290 --> 00:00:26.259
has chipped away at
the independence of the court,

00:00:26.259 --> 00:00:28.995
and has implemented a crackdown
on immigration that has made him

00:00:28.995 --> 00:00:31.530
a pariah in Europe,
or as Trump put it...

00:00:31.530 --> 00:00:35.000
-Viktor Orbán has done
a tremendous job

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:37.670
in so many different ways.
Highly respected.

00:00:37.670 --> 00:00:40.707
Respected all over Europe.

00:00:40.707 --> 00:00:44.043
Probably, like me, a little bit
controversial, but that's okay.

00:00:44.043 --> 00:00:45.879
That's okay.

00:00:45.879 --> 00:00:48.247
-A little bit controversial

00:00:48.247 --> 00:00:50.483
is not how you describe
a wannabe dictator.

00:00:50.483 --> 00:00:53.219
That's how your aunt describes

00:00:53.219 --> 00:00:55.421
"50 Shades of Grey."
[ Laughter ]

00:00:55.421 --> 00:00:57.423
That's a little bit
controversial, but that's okay.

00:00:57.423 --> 00:00:59.725
They're having fun.

00:00:59.725 --> 00:01:01.027
But while Trump was palling
around with

00:01:01.027 --> 00:01:02.261
the authoritarian leader
of Hungary,

00:01:02.261 --> 00:01:04.397
he was also conducting
a trade war with China.

00:01:04.397 --> 00:01:07.066
Today China said it would impose
retaliatory tariffs

00:01:07.066 --> 00:01:09.669
against the U.S., and the stock
market plummeted as a result.

00:01:09.669 --> 00:01:11.838
But Trump shrugged it off,
suggesting our economy

00:01:11.838 --> 00:01:13.939
was strong enough to handle it
while, as usual,

00:01:13.939 --> 00:01:15.407
sounding incredibly vague.

00:01:15.407 --> 00:01:16.675
-We're in a very strong
position.

00:01:16.675 --> 00:01:18.344
Our economy has been
very powerful.

00:01:18.344 --> 00:01:19.679
Theirs has not been.

00:01:19.679 --> 00:01:23.883
We've gone up a lot since
our great election in 2016,

00:01:23.883 --> 00:01:28.120
and if you look at the numbers,
they've gone down quite a bit.

00:01:28.120 --> 00:01:29.755
We're dealing with them.

00:01:29.755 --> 00:01:31.157
We have a very good
relationship.

00:01:31.157 --> 00:01:32.692
Maybe something will happen.

00:01:32.692 --> 00:01:36.162
-Maybe something will happen?

00:01:36.162 --> 00:01:38.597
Sounds like a Mafia boss
doing a book report

00:01:38.597 --> 00:01:40.533
on a book he's never even
heard of.

00:01:40.533 --> 00:01:42.367
[ Mobster accent ]
"To Kill A Mockingbird,"

00:01:42.367 --> 00:01:43.836
it's about a mockingbird.

00:01:43.836 --> 00:01:45.738
He owes some people some money,
maybe something bad happen.

00:01:45.738 --> 00:01:47.307
Maybe the mockingbird
had it coming. Capiche?

00:01:47.307 --> 00:01:48.541
[ Laughter ]

00:01:48.541 --> 00:01:50.042
Let's just say
you don't got to worry about

00:01:50.042 --> 00:01:51.644
anybody mocking anymore.

00:01:51.644 --> 00:01:53.112
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:53.112 --> 00:01:56.448
[ Normal voice ] Trump casts
himself as a master deal maker,

00:01:56.448 --> 00:01:57.817
but what we're learning
yet again

00:01:57.817 --> 00:01:59.585
is that he's actually terrible
at making deals.

00:01:59.585 --> 00:02:02.488
This is what Trump does --
He creates myths about himself

00:02:02.488 --> 00:02:03.689
until the truth comes out.

00:02:03.689 --> 00:02:06.025
Like how he brags about
his prowess at golf.

00:02:06.025 --> 00:02:07.560
For example, you might remember

00:02:07.560 --> 00:02:09.695
the time Trump held a round
table of CEOs

00:02:09.695 --> 00:02:11.964
on how to bring back
manufacturing jobs

00:02:11.964 --> 00:02:14.199
and made the CEO
of General Electric tell a story

00:02:14.199 --> 00:02:16.535
about how Trump
supposedly hit a hole in one.

00:02:16.535 --> 00:02:17.970
-Mr. President, good to see
you again. Jeff Immelt, G.E.

00:02:17.970 --> 00:02:20.072
-Hi, Jeff.
-Great to be here.

00:02:20.072 --> 00:02:21.407
Look forward to really working
with you

00:02:21.407 --> 00:02:22.942
on creating more manufacturing
jobs.

00:02:22.942 --> 00:02:24.710
-Jeff actually watched me
make a hole in one.

00:02:24.710 --> 00:02:27.246
Can you believe that?
Should you tell that story?

00:02:27.246 --> 00:02:28.347
[ Laughter ]

00:02:28.347 --> 00:02:30.850
-We were trying to
talk President Trump

00:02:30.850 --> 00:02:32.251
into doing "The Apprentice."

00:02:32.251 --> 00:02:34.420
That was my assignment
when we owned NBC.

00:02:34.420 --> 00:02:37.890
President Trump goes up to
a par 3 on his course,

00:02:37.890 --> 00:02:40.360
he looks to the three of us
and says,

00:02:40.360 --> 00:02:42.628
"You realize, of course, I'm the
richest golfer in the world."

00:02:42.628 --> 00:02:46.399
That's a comment,
then gets a hole in one.

00:02:46.399 --> 00:02:47.733
[ Laughter ]

00:02:47.733 --> 00:02:51.403
-Crazy.
-I have to say, you know,

00:02:51.403 --> 00:02:53.940
I've seen the magic before.
So --

00:02:53.940 --> 00:02:57.710
[ laughter ]
-It's so crazy. It's so crazy.

00:02:57.710 --> 00:02:59.779
No, I actually said I was
the best golfer

00:02:59.779 --> 00:03:03.782
of all the rich people,
to be exact.

00:03:03.782 --> 00:03:06.518
-[ Laughs haughtily ]

00:03:06.518 --> 00:03:09.755
[ Laughing continues ]

00:03:09.755 --> 00:03:11.924
I spit out my caviar.

00:03:11.924 --> 00:03:14.393
[ Laughter ]

00:03:14.393 --> 00:03:19.064
[ Applause ]
Just a true -- right there.

00:03:19.064 --> 00:03:21.467
You have it,
a true man of the people.

00:03:21.467 --> 00:03:24.337
A billionaire president
who cheats on his taxes

00:03:24.337 --> 00:03:26.405
yucking it up with
a bunch of wealthy CEOs

00:03:26.405 --> 00:03:28.641
and bragging about how he's
the richest golfer in the world.

00:03:28.641 --> 00:03:31.210
It's like an episode
of the "Twilight Zone"

00:03:31.210 --> 00:03:33.446
written by Bernie Sanders.

00:03:33.446 --> 00:03:35.881
[ As Sanders ] Imagine if will,
a golfer,

00:03:35.881 --> 00:03:38.618
but this is no ordinary golfer.

00:03:38.618 --> 00:03:43.856
He's also the president, and
the CEO of the "Twilight Zone."

00:03:43.856 --> 00:03:46.158
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:46.158 --> 00:03:50.930
Roll the episode.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:50.930 --> 00:03:53.032
There's a twist at the end.

00:03:53.032 --> 00:03:54.767
There's no hole.

00:03:54.767 --> 00:03:56.969
[ Laughter ]

00:03:56.969 --> 00:03:59.472
That's the twist. He --
Just golfing, there's no hole.

00:03:59.472 --> 00:04:01.474
[ Laughter ]

00:04:01.474 --> 00:04:05.411
Pretty good twist.

00:04:05.411 --> 00:04:07.713
[ Normal voice ] Now we all know
Trump cheats at golf.

00:04:07.713 --> 00:04:08.915
He's notorious for it.

00:04:08.915 --> 00:04:11.017
In fact, there's
an entire book about it

00:04:11.017 --> 00:04:12.651
called "Commander in Cheat."

00:04:12.651 --> 00:04:14.053
That book came out last month,

00:04:14.053 --> 00:04:16.355
which means it came out the same
month as the Mueller report.

00:04:16.355 --> 00:04:18.191
A book about cheating
at politics,

00:04:18.191 --> 00:04:20.126
and a book about cheating
at golf.

00:04:20.126 --> 00:04:22.562
This guy cheats so much,
he had two separate books

00:04:22.562 --> 00:04:24.363
about cheating come out
in the same month.

00:04:24.363 --> 00:04:27.333
Soon, it's going to be its own
section at Barnes &amp; Noble.

00:04:27.333 --> 00:04:29.034
They'll be books,
"Cheating in Marriage,"

00:04:29.034 --> 00:04:33.605
there'll be
"Cheating in School."

00:04:33.605 --> 00:04:36.108
He'll have a book like,
"Cheating in Cooking."

00:04:36.108 --> 00:04:38.377
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:38.377 --> 00:04:40.213
And the sportswriter
who wrote the golf book

00:04:40.213 --> 00:04:43.316
said last month on CNN that it
wasn't just the occasional game.

00:04:43.316 --> 00:04:45.618
Trump cheats in brazen
and bewildering ways

00:04:45.618 --> 00:04:48.354
even when he's playing the best
golfers in the world.

00:04:48.354 --> 00:04:49.855
-You're not just saying
he cheats.

00:04:49.855 --> 00:04:52.124
You're saying he cheats!

00:04:52.124 --> 00:04:55.028
I mean he cheats on all of it.

00:04:55.028 --> 00:04:57.230
-He cheats like
a Mafia accountant.

00:04:57.230 --> 00:04:58.998
He cheats crazy.

00:04:58.998 --> 00:05:00.566
He cheats whether
you're watching or not.

00:05:00.566 --> 00:05:02.101
He cheats whether
you like it or not.

00:05:02.101 --> 00:05:05.037
He tried to cheat Tiger Woods
in a match.

00:05:05.037 --> 00:05:08.073
Tiger hits it like this.
He hits two balls in the water,

00:05:08.073 --> 00:05:09.274
doesn't count either,

00:05:09.274 --> 00:05:12.177
and pretends that he almost tied
Tiger Woods.

00:05:12.177 --> 00:05:14.314
-He tried to cheat against Tiger
Woods.

00:05:14.314 --> 00:05:16.415
That's like challenging
LeBron James

00:05:16.415 --> 00:05:19.085
to a slam dunk contest
and bringing a ladder.

00:05:19.085 --> 00:05:20.286
[ Laughter ]

00:05:20.286 --> 00:05:21.821
[ As Trump ]
So I guess it's a draw.

00:05:21.821 --> 00:05:23.789
Both dunked.

00:05:23.789 --> 00:05:25.257
[ Normal voice ]
And then last week we got maybe

00:05:25.257 --> 00:05:27.860
the craziest cheating story yet
from that same author

00:05:27.860 --> 00:05:29.528
involving a guy named
Ted Virtue,

00:05:29.528 --> 00:05:31.564
the CEO of
a New York investment firm.

00:05:31.564 --> 00:05:34.333
Virtue was at Trump's golf
course in Florida with his son.

00:05:34.333 --> 00:05:37.537
Now this was while Trump
was already president.

00:05:37.537 --> 00:05:39.939
Here's how the story starts.
Trump sees Ted on the 9th hole

00:05:39.939 --> 00:05:41.340
and decides to drive his cart
over.

00:05:41.340 --> 00:05:43.643
He tells Ted, "Congrats on
winning the club championship.

00:05:43.643 --> 00:05:46.078
But you didn't really win it,
because I was out of town."

00:05:46.078 --> 00:05:48.080
And if you're curious
where Trump was

00:05:48.080 --> 00:05:49.548
when he says was out of town,

00:05:49.548 --> 00:05:52.952
Trump was meeting with
Kim Jong-un in Singapore.

00:05:52.952 --> 00:05:55.354
This guy was at
a high-stakes nuclear summit

00:05:55.354 --> 00:05:56.822
with the leader
of a rogue nation

00:05:56.822 --> 00:06:00.526
all bummed out he was missing
the club tournament.

00:06:00.526 --> 00:06:02.728
Can you imagine the amount
of whining and moaning

00:06:02.728 --> 00:06:04.396
Kim Jong-un had to put up with?

00:06:04.396 --> 00:06:06.466
[ As Trump ] You better disarm,
because while I'm here,

00:06:06.466 --> 00:06:08.934
Ted Virtue is winning
my tournament.

00:06:08.934 --> 00:06:11.270
Translate that.
Translate that to him.

00:06:11.270 --> 00:06:13.638
And tell him Ted Virtue's
a real jerk. Say it.

00:06:13.638 --> 00:06:15.674
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:06:15.674 --> 00:06:18.944
[ Normal voice ] But the story
gets weirder from there.

00:06:18.944 --> 00:06:21.113
Because Trump challenged Virtue
and his son

00:06:21.113 --> 00:06:23.516
to play for the club
championship on the spot.

00:06:23.516 --> 00:06:25.952
They get to a hole with a big
pond in front of the green.

00:06:25.952 --> 00:06:28.054
Both Ted and his son hit
the ball on the green,

00:06:28.054 --> 00:06:29.655
but Trump hits his in the water.

00:06:29.655 --> 00:06:30.889
By the time they
get to the hole though,

00:06:30.889 --> 00:06:32.491
Trump is lining up the son's
ball.

00:06:32.491 --> 00:06:35.628
Only now it's his ball,
and the caddy has switched it.

00:06:35.628 --> 00:06:37.163
The son is like,
"That's my ball."

00:06:37.163 --> 00:06:39.465
But Trump's caddy goes "No,
this is the president's ball.

00:06:39.465 --> 00:06:41.200
Your ball went in the water."

00:06:41.200 --> 00:06:43.001
Ted and his son look at each
other confused,

00:06:43.001 --> 00:06:45.804
not sure if this is
really happening.

00:06:45.804 --> 00:06:48.207
Oh, it's happening.

00:06:48.207 --> 00:06:50.843
Everything you're not sure of
is happening.

00:06:50.843 --> 00:06:52.444
But this is what Trump does.

00:06:52.444 --> 00:06:53.880
On stuff as big as a trade

00:06:53.880 --> 00:06:55.614
or as small as a ball
hit in the water,

00:06:55.614 --> 00:06:57.483
he makes you question
your sense of reality.

00:06:57.483 --> 00:06:59.919
He's like a guy who only
kind of knows

00:06:59.919 --> 00:07:01.587
how to jedi mind trick you.

00:07:01.587 --> 00:07:03.088
But instead of actually
convincing you,

00:07:03.088 --> 00:07:06.359
he just keeps saying it until
you get irritated and give up.

00:07:06.359 --> 00:07:07.860
[ As Trump ] This is not
the ball you're looking for.

00:07:07.860 --> 00:07:09.328
[ Normal voice ] No, yeah,
that is actually my ball.

00:07:09.328 --> 00:07:10.462
[ As Trump ] No, it's not.

00:07:10.462 --> 00:07:11.563
[ Normal voice ]
Yeah, no, it definitely is.

00:07:11.563 --> 00:07:12.398
[ As Trump ] No, it's not.

00:07:12.398 --> 00:07:13.165
[ Normal voice ] Yeah, it is.

00:07:13.165 --> 00:07:14.333
[ As Trump ] No, it's not.

00:07:14.333 --> 00:07:15.468
[ Normal voice ]
Fine, whatever. Just take it.

00:07:15.468 --> 00:07:17.937
[ As Trump ]
You just got jedied.

00:07:17.937 --> 00:07:19.505
[ Normal voice ] But there's
a revealing part of this story,

00:07:19.505 --> 00:07:21.974
and it involves what happens
when Trump actually tries

00:07:21.974 --> 00:07:25.845
to play in regulated matches
with rules where he can't cheat.

00:07:25.845 --> 00:07:28.214
This will shock you --
He's not nearly as good.

00:07:28.214 --> 00:07:30.383
-He's played on television
ten times,

00:07:30.383 --> 00:07:32.418
Pebble Beach Pro-Am seven times,

00:07:32.418 --> 00:07:34.653
and the Lake Tahoe thing
three times.

00:07:34.653 --> 00:07:37.256
He has never made the cut
at Pebble Beach,

00:07:37.256 --> 00:07:39.792
and at Tahoe, he's never
finished in the top half.

00:07:39.792 --> 00:07:41.927
So when there's rules guys
and cameras,

00:07:41.927 --> 00:07:43.562
he's not that good.

00:07:43.562 --> 00:07:45.998
When it's just his course,
his caddy, his world,

00:07:45.998 --> 00:07:47.500
he's pretty good.

00:07:47.500 --> 00:07:48.901
-In fact, as a general rule

00:07:48.901 --> 00:07:50.569
I would say Donald Trump
looks much worse

00:07:50.569 --> 00:07:53.305
when there are cameras than
when there are not.

00:07:53.305 --> 00:07:56.775
On paper, Trump is a 6'3"
self-made business genius

00:07:56.775 --> 00:07:58.711
worth $10 billion
who went to Wharton,

00:07:58.711 --> 00:08:00.646
lives in a gold tower,
and won a presidential election,

00:08:00.646 --> 00:08:02.614
but on camera,
he's a guy who openly colludes

00:08:02.614 --> 00:08:03.983
with foreign adversaries,

00:08:03.983 --> 00:08:06.285
sweats like he's chugging
hot sauce at end of a marathon,

00:08:06.285 --> 00:08:09.488
and can't pronounce words that
are longer than two syllables.

00:08:09.488 --> 00:08:11.123
-Every single car out there,

00:08:11.123 --> 00:08:13.092
even the really expenses ones...

00:08:13.092 --> 00:08:15.294
Controlled by large derners.

00:08:15.294 --> 00:08:19.131
10,000 known or suspested
gang members.

00:08:19.131 --> 00:08:20.866
[ Laughter ]
-Suspested.

00:08:20.866 --> 00:08:23.969
As in everyone suspested
that Trump cheats at golf,

00:08:23.969 --> 00:08:25.904
but now we're positrive.

00:08:25.904 --> 00:08:27.673
[ Laughter, cheers,
and applause ]

00:08:27.673 --> 00:08:31.310
But here's the thing,
you guys...

00:08:31.310 --> 00:08:34.680
Trump might be
the most prolific cheater

00:08:34.680 --> 00:08:36.315
in the Republican Party,
but he's not alone.

00:08:36.315 --> 00:08:38.183
The ranks of the GOP
are filled with guys

00:08:38.183 --> 00:08:40.453
who know they can only win
if they cheat,

00:08:40.453 --> 00:08:41.954
which is why
they're so dedicated

00:08:41.954 --> 00:08:44.490
to passing voter suppression
laws, stacking the courts,

00:08:44.490 --> 00:08:46.091
and accepting the help
of foreign countries

00:08:46.091 --> 00:08:47.359
interfering in our elections.

00:08:47.359 --> 00:08:48.494
In fact, over the weekend,

00:08:48.494 --> 00:08:50.362
we got some news
of a very bizarre plot

00:08:50.362 --> 00:08:52.297
by Trump's lawyer,
Rudy Giuliani,

00:08:52.297 --> 00:08:54.867
to go to Ukraine and seek
their help in the 2020 election.

00:08:54.867 --> 00:08:57.702
-President Trump's personal
attorney, Rudy Giuliani,

00:08:57.702 --> 00:09:00.105
planning to travel
to Ukraine soon.

00:09:00.105 --> 00:09:02.808
"The New York Times" reports
he will ask that country's

00:09:02.808 --> 00:09:04.877
new president to investigate
the origin

00:09:04.877 --> 00:09:07.512
of special counsel Mueller's
Russia investigation.

00:09:07.512 --> 00:09:09.949
Giuliani will also press Ukraine
to look into

00:09:09.949 --> 00:09:13.819
Joe Biden's son's involvement
in a gas company

00:09:13.819 --> 00:09:16.622
owned by a Ukrainian oligarch.

00:09:16.622 --> 00:09:19.558
-So, Rudy's plan was to fly
to Ukraine and dig up dirt

00:09:19.558 --> 00:09:21.259
on the Russia probe
and Joe Biden?

00:09:21.259 --> 00:09:23.162
First of all, you don't need
to go to Ukraine

00:09:23.162 --> 00:09:24.363
to dig up dirt on Biden.

00:09:24.363 --> 00:09:26.265
There are actual pictures
of the dude sniffing hair

00:09:26.265 --> 00:09:28.467
and rubbing shoulders,
and by the way,

00:09:28.467 --> 00:09:30.436
it's not like this wasn't
weird at the time.

00:09:30.436 --> 00:09:32.772
I mean look at the faces
of the dudes on either side.

00:09:32.772 --> 00:09:38.210
They're like,
"Uhhhh, should we go?"

00:09:38.210 --> 00:09:40.245
Second,
think about how crazy this is --

00:09:40.245 --> 00:09:42.814
the president's lawyer is now
just openly inviting

00:09:42.814 --> 00:09:44.450
the interference
of foreign governments

00:09:44.450 --> 00:09:46.184
to dig up dirt
on political opponents.

00:09:46.184 --> 00:09:48.854
Rudy basically even admitted it
when he told "The Times"

00:09:48.854 --> 00:09:50.355
we're not meddling
in an election,

00:09:50.355 --> 00:09:51.891
we're meddling in an
investigation,

00:09:51.891 --> 00:09:53.425
which we have a right to do.

00:09:53.425 --> 00:09:54.993
There's nothing illegal
about it.

00:09:54.993 --> 00:09:56.962
Somebody could say,
it's improper.

00:09:56.962 --> 00:09:58.330
All right. I'll say it.

00:09:58.330 --> 00:10:00.498
It's improper.

00:10:00.498 --> 00:10:03.101
The best thing about Rudy
is he just admits everything.

00:10:03.101 --> 00:10:05.337
We probably wouldn't have needed
the Mueller report

00:10:05.337 --> 00:10:07.640
if we had just given Rudy
a podcast.

00:10:07.640 --> 00:10:10.075
[ Laughter ]

00:10:10.075 --> 00:10:12.978
After the story broke,
Rudy went on Fox News

00:10:12.978 --> 00:10:14.847
to announce that he wasn't
going to Ukraine after all.

00:10:14.847 --> 00:10:16.515
But the weirdest part of
the interview was when

00:10:16.515 --> 00:10:19.919
the anchor tried to end it,
and Rudy would not stop talking,

00:10:19.919 --> 00:10:21.620
up until the point where
the anchor pointed out

00:10:21.620 --> 00:10:24.256
that he was accidentally
making more news.

00:10:24.256 --> 00:10:27.593
-I am actually quite confident
that the facts with regard

00:10:27.593 --> 00:10:30.629
to Vice President --
former Vice President Biden

00:10:30.629 --> 00:10:33.532
are so compelling that there's
no way he gets from here

00:10:33.532 --> 00:10:36.068
to the election without this
being investigated.

00:10:36.068 --> 00:10:38.370
-Okay, so --
-Tell me if this wouldn't be

00:10:38.370 --> 00:10:41.573
major news if it were
the Trumps.

00:10:41.573 --> 00:10:43.442
-Mr. Mayor, we're out of time,
but listen --

00:10:43.442 --> 00:10:46.712
-Don't bother to answer.
Just have your viewers answer.

00:10:46.712 --> 00:10:48.547
-For now, we'll let
the world know

00:10:48.547 --> 00:10:50.449
you're not headed to Ukraine.
-Right now, I'm not going.

00:10:50.449 --> 00:10:51.950
-Alright.
-So they can call me for it --

00:10:51.950 --> 00:10:54.153
-We're out of time.
-And maybe I'll take

00:10:54.153 --> 00:10:55.620
executive privilege
or something or other.

00:10:55.620 --> 00:10:57.022
-Oh, boy. Oh, boy.
-I don't know. We'll see.

00:10:57.022 --> 00:10:58.423
Or maybe I'll testify.
-You're making another headline

00:10:58.423 --> 00:11:00.025
tonight Mr. Mayor.
-Let's see what can happen,

00:11:00.025 --> 00:11:01.327
but --
-Thank you for dropping in.

00:11:01.327 --> 00:11:03.295
-They are really pathetic.
-We have to go.

00:11:03.295 --> 00:11:05.097
-And they're scared,
and they're on defense.

00:11:05.097 --> 00:11:06.632
-Alright, we got to go.
Thank you for dropping in.

00:11:06.632 --> 00:11:07.600
Great to see you.

00:11:07.600 --> 00:11:09.502
-Oh, my God, Rudy!

00:11:09.502 --> 00:11:12.137
Rudy did not want that interview
to end.

00:11:12.137 --> 00:11:13.605
[ As Giuliani ] Please don't
send me back to the home!

00:11:13.605 --> 00:11:15.307
The nurses are mean to me!

00:11:15.307 --> 00:11:16.842
[ Laughter ]

00:11:16.842 --> 00:11:20.546
Also, only a Fox anchor

00:11:20.546 --> 00:11:22.715
would express shock
and disappointment

00:11:22.715 --> 00:11:23.949
at making another headline.

00:11:23.949 --> 00:11:25.885
You just got
the president's personal lawyer

00:11:25.885 --> 00:11:28.253
to say that he might invoke
executive privilege

00:11:28.253 --> 00:11:30.589
if asked about a foreign trip
to dig up dirt on

00:11:30.589 --> 00:11:32.791
a political opponent to meddle
in a presidential campaign.

00:11:32.791 --> 00:11:35.294
Meaning, he's discussed that
plan with the president himself.

00:11:35.294 --> 00:11:38.664
Fox anchors react to news like
when your 5-year-old admits

00:11:38.664 --> 00:11:40.465
too much when you get to
a birthday party.

00:11:40.465 --> 00:11:43.201
We're late because we stopped
at the store with bottles

00:11:43.201 --> 00:11:44.470
to buy some daddy juice.

00:11:44.470 --> 00:11:46.305
Alright. That's --

00:11:46.305 --> 00:11:49.040
That's enough.
That's not for them to know.

00:11:49.040 --> 00:11:51.009
But this is what it's like
inside the bubble --

00:11:51.009 --> 00:11:53.278
whether it's cheating at golf
or cheating at politics,

00:11:53.278 --> 00:11:55.014
when these guys are in
their own little world,

00:11:55.014 --> 00:11:56.482
they operate by their own rules.

00:11:56.482 --> 00:11:59.085
That's why Trump has so much
affection for strongmen.

00:11:59.085 --> 00:12:01.520
He thinks he's above the law,
or as fox news would put it,

00:12:01.520 --> 00:12:03.122
he's...
-A little bit controversial,

00:12:03.122 --> 00:12:04.556
but that's okay.

00:12:04.556 --> 00:12:06.258
-This has been "A Closer Look."

00:12:06.258 --> 00:12:07.392
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:12:07.392 --> 00:12:08.894 line:0%
♪♪

